---
layout: default
title: Series
permalink: /series/
sitemap_priority: 0.7
sitemap_changefreq: weekly
description: >-
  Every Software Architecture Insights series in one place — multi-part runs
  on AI-native architecture, AI and the developer, AI ethics, security,
  availability, and cloud migration.
---

<%
  # Curated order, not computed: `order` in src/_data/series.yml is editorial
  # judgment about which series matters most. Entries without an `order` sort
  # last rather than blowing up, so adding a series to the YAML without
  # deciding its rank still builds.
  articles_by_series = site.collections.articles.resources
    .select { |r| r.data.series }
    .group_by { |r| r.data.series }

  series_list = site.data.series.sort_by { |s| s["order"] || 999 }
%>

<header class="listing-header">
  <h1>Series</h1>
  <p class="listing-description">
    Some of these were written as a planned run, start to finish. Others are
    articles that turned out to be one argument spread over a couple of years.
    Either way, they read best together.
  </p>
</header>

<ol class="series-index">
  <% series_list.each do |series| %>
    <%
      articles = (articles_by_series[series["label"]] || []).sort_by { |r| r.data.date }
      next if articles.empty?
      first, last = articles.first.data.date, articles.last.data.date
      span = if first.strftime("%Y") == last.strftime("%Y")
               first.strftime("%Y")
             else
               "#{first.strftime('%Y')}&ndash;#{last.strftime('%Y')}"
             end
    %>
    <li class="series-index-item">
      <a href="<%= relative_url "/series/#{series['key']}/" %>" class="series-index-title"><%= series["label"] %></a>
      <p class="series-index-meta">
        <%= articles.length %> <%= articles.length == 1 ? "article" : "articles" %>
        &middot; <%= span %>
      </p>
      <p class="series-index-description"><%= series["description"] %></p>
      <a href="<%= relative_url "/series/#{series['key']}/" %>" class="article-list-readmore">Read the series &rarr;</a>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ol>
